From: Codex <codex@openai.com>
Subject: [PATCH] provide A37 netd resolver library from M4 tethering APEX

# Reason: attempt0207 repeats `CANNOT LINK EXECUTABLE "/system/bin/netd": library "libnetd_resolv.so" not found`; target-files SYSTEM netd needs the DSO, while the S22-based diagnostic APEX composition omitted it. BZI6 contains the hash-pinned provider and its apex_manifest.pb exports it through provideNativeLibs.
# Affected: diagnostic-only APEX composition helper and lock in the existing Exynos9810 restore module. Normal M4 profile and donor/native/RIL/vendor payloads remain unchanged.
# Verify: exact donor lib hash; protobuf field-7 export; five-file-only payload diff; UID/GID/mode/SELinux metadata; ext4 roundtrip; AVB, v3, 4KiB alignment; repeat build exact APEX hash; postboot diagnostic verifier pins exact output. Device network behavior remains a separate runtime gate.
# Rollback: reverse patch0207 and rebuild the previous M4 diagnostic artifact; retained attempt37 and attempt0207 remain unchanged. No kernel, modem, EFS or protected partition change.

